~ start
if Global.wife_dialogue_progress == 1 and Global.has_wedding_ring:
	PC: Is this yours?

	W: …
	W: Do you remember?

	PC: Remember? Remember what?

	W: On the couch, you laid.
	W: A sickly smell that filled the air. 
	W: When did we lose what once was?

	#Flashback

	W: Welcome home, {{Global.father_name}}.

	PC: …

	W: Are you-?
	W: Drunk again, I see. 

	PC: Do you want some? *Hic* 

	W: …do you remember what day it is today?

	PC: Uh…monday. 

	W: And?

	PC: Bah, what are these questions?
	PC: I don’t care. 

	W: …

	#End Flashback

	W: It was our anniversary.
	W: Did you remember? 

	W: …or did you not care? 

	PC: I…
	PC: (What the hell was that?)
	PC: (That was me talking? Why?)
	PC: (I’m missing something…but what?)
	PC: (It must be somewhere here in the car…)
	$> Global.wife_dialogue_progress = 2
	=> END
elif Global.wife_dialogue_progress == 2 and Global.has_alcohol_bottle:
	PC: This…is what I drank?
	PC: It’s cheap. 

	W: It used to be wine. 
	W: Dare I say, perhaps it was an improvement. 
	W: Though that isn’t saying much at all, isn’t it?

	#Flashback 

	W: When would you stop drinking?
	W: It certainly isn’t making your liver any better. 

	PC: Piss off! I do what I want. 

	W: I’m worried about you. 

	PC: I don’t give a rat’s ass about your worry - hic. 
	PC: Now leave me alone. 

	W: {{Global.father_name}}...

	PC: I said leave me alone!

	#End Flashback

	$> Global.wife_dialogue_progress = 3
	=> final
elif Global.wife_dialogue_progress == 3:
	~ final
	W: You used to be a better person. 
	W: You used to be the man I loved. 
	W: But tell me, do you even remember what you did?
	W: What you have done?

	PC: I do know you. 

	W: You thought you did. 
	
	$> Global.reveal_charcter("Wife")
	
	PC: {{Global.wife_name}}! God, I didn’t recognize you!

	W It’s been years since I last recognized you.
	
	W: If marriage is made of love, then what happens when there is none?
	W: When you left me then, alone with the sickly smell, I wondered.

	W: Perhaps this marriage is no longer one of love, but one of emptiness and one of hate. 

	PC: Don’t say such ridiculous things. You’re my wife. You have your duties, and I have mine. That’s what holds the family together.

	W: I can’t bear to see this side of you. It’s this side of you that tore us apart.
	W: I didn’t used to hate you. 
	W: I loved you once. 
	W: But even that…has frosted over. 

	PC So that’s how you feel, is it? Well, no that you’ve called down, I’m sure we can work something out. I know you will see things my way.

	W: I’ve already made up my mind. I was just waiting for the chance to give you these.
 
	$> Global.has_divorce_papers = true

	PC: …
	W: The door is open. 
	W: You should go. 

	=> END
elif Global.wife_dialogue_progress == 0:
	W: …welcome home, {{Global.father_name}}.

	PC: What? How do you–
	PC: (How do they know my name?)

	PC: Who are you?

	W: …
	W: Welcome home…

	PC: (This is disturbing to look at.)
	$> Global.wife_dialogue_progress = 1
	=> END
elif Global.wife_dialogue_progress == 1:
	W: …welcome home, {{Global.father_name}}.
	PC: (This is disturbing to look at.)
else:
	PC: (I’m missing something…but what?)